<title>MEXICO: Mexico's vehicle production up slightly Jan-May.</title>
<headline>Mexico's vehicle production up slightly Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's automobile industry produced 528,092 vehicles during the first five months of the year versus 506,111 units produced during the same period of 1995, a rise of 4.3 percent, the Mexican Automobile Industry Association (AMIA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Mexico also exported 393,043 units during the year's first five months versus 412,497, a decline of 4.7 percent during the year-ago period.</p>
<p>National sales in the January-May period reached 162,103 units, up 38.4 percent, from the 117,137 units in the same period a year ago.  </p>
<p>The following table compares production and sales data for cars and trucks and buses during the relevant periods.</p>
<p>				    JAN-MAY 97	    JAN-MAY 96</p>
<p>    TOTAL PRODUCTION	     528,092		  506,111</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC MARKET	 130,357		   88,982</p>
<p>		autos		   92,868		   58,190</p>
<p>		trucks and buses    37,489		   30,792</p>
<p>	   EXPORT MARKET	   397,735		  417,129</p>
<p>    DOMESTIC SALES		 162,103		  117,137</p>
<p>    TOTAL EXPORTS		  393,043		  412,497</p>
<p>		autos		  239,567		  277,186</p>
<p>		trucks and buses   153,476		  135,311</p>
<p>    DOMESTIC RETAIL SALES	156,804		  111,957</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289530))</p>
